        <mxCell id="Pu6BV0exmzuBZcvi8_VK-137" edge="1" parent="1" source="Pu6BV0exmzuBZcvi8_VK-10" style="shape=link;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="Pu6BV0exmzuBZcvi8_VK-91" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" width="100" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="1490" y="1319.17" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="1150" y="1319.17" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Pu6BV0exmzuBZcvi8_VK-138" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assumptions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;USD/EUR rates are derived, not stored — the question just says rates are specified in three currencies; it doesn&#39;t say how. We assumed only the LKR rate is stored, and USD/EUR are calculated by applying a live exchange rate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Guest only exists once a booking happens — the question doesn&#39;t say this explicitly. We assumed &quot;Guest&quot; as an entity is scoped to people who book a room (hence total participation in Books), meaning someone who only orders food without ever booking a room falls outside this model.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Age is a derived attribute — the question asks for age to be stored but doesn&#39;t say how it&#39;s obtained. We assumed it&#39;s calculated from Date of Birth rather than entered independently (even though the ER shows it as stored).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Food order charges are derived — the question says guests are charged based on food type and quantity, but doesn&#39;t specify a formula. We assumed charges = quantity × menu item price, calculated rather than manually entered.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The no-double-booking rule is enforced as a data constraint, not a structural ER element — the question states the rule directly, but since crow&#39;s-foot/Chen cardinalities can&#39;t express &quot;no overlapping dates for the same room,&quot; we assumed this gets handled as a uniqueness constraint on Booking (Room + date range) at implementation time.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="740" width="900" x="-1440" y="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
